From: Kotesh Murugan <koteshlost@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] dualopend: zero-init main state to silence UBSan on reconnected

Crash signature (Nyx, AFL++, dual_funding scenario, CLN v25.12.1):

    runtime error: load of value 254, which is not a valid value for type 'bool'
    openingd/dualopend.c: in main()                  state->reconnected

`state->reconnected` is read on the first peer message before any code path
assigns it, because `tal()` returns uninitialised memory. UBSan trips on
the garbage byte; the crash handler reports it via Nyx and the snapshot
resets. Switching to `talz()` zero-initialises the whole struct, which is
what every other dualopend code path already assumes.

---
 openingd/dualopend.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/openingd/dualopend.c b/openingd/dualopend.c
--- a/openingd/dualopend.c
+++ b/openingd/dualopend.c
@@ -4340,7 +4340,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	setup_locale();

 	struct pollfd pollfd[2];
-	struct state *state = tal(NULL, struct state);
+	struct state *state = talz(NULL, struct state);
 	struct fee_states *fee_states;
 	enum side opener;
 	u8 *msg;
